node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/

# What a run of the suite leaves for `.github/why-it-went-red/` to read. An artifact of a
# run, like coverage/ above: rewritten by every run and never reviewed.
why-it-went-red.json

# The before-listing `.github/what-the-suite-left-behind/` takes with the suite stopped. A fact
# about one machine at one instant: committed, every sweep after the first reads a stranger's /tmp.
what-the-suite-left-behind.json
*.log
*.tgz
.DS_Store

# The second reader of the chain format is Python (packages/chain/verifier/), so this
# tree has bytecode caches now. They are build output, like dist/ above.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local AI-assistant state (permissions, plans).
.claude/

# Reconstruction workbench (local-only; see .refactor/README.md).
.refactor/

# Alpha-era local-only artifacts kept out of the reconstruction (referenced
# from the `main` branch; not part of the rebuilt tree).
AGENTS.md
docs-local/
scripts/

# Dogfood: mnema runs against itself in this repo, so this .mnema/ is a
# development workbench, not a reference project — ignored WHOLESALE.
#
# This is a deliberate exception for the tool's OWN repo. Adopter projects do
# the opposite (and `mnema init` scaffolds a .gitignore that commits the chain
# and public keys, ignoring only the rebuildable state/cache and the private
# key). The faithful examples of the audit flow are those adopter repos, never
# this one.
.mnema/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HELD-OUT TASK OUTPUTS — P1 round 1, and only round 1.
#
# `measurements/p1/split.json` names six held-out tasks. Their raw output and
# their diffs DESCRIBE the task, so committing them publishes the task before
# the reveal. 312 such files sat untracked-and-unignored in this tree for three
# days, where one `git add -A` would have published them — which this project
# has already done once.
#
# IGNORED BY NAME, one line per task per run, never by a wildcard over `raw/`
# or `diffs/`: the DEVELOPMENT tasks' outputs live in those same directories
# and ARE committed (`a1-rounding`, `a3-idempotency`), and a directory-wide
# ignore would silently stop committing the next one.
#
# UNTIL WHEN: these lines are DELETED — not amended, not widened — on the day
# the six tasks are published in `measurements/p1/`. Nothing else retires them,
# and an ignore with no end written on it is an ignore nobody removes.
#
# ROUNDS 2 AND 3 NEED NO LINES HERE. Checked 21/08/2026: their held-out raw
# output and diffs are not on disk at all, and every raw/diff they do track
# belongs to a development task.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# round 1 · 2026-08-18-full
measurements/p1/results/2026-08-18-full/raw/a2-due-day-*
measurements/p1/results/2026-08-18-full/diffs/a2-due-day-*
